# Copy to warp-team.env and fill in. Enrols the rig's WARP device in a
# Zero Trust organisation headlessly, through /var/lib/cloudflare-warp/mdm.xml.
#
# WARP_ORG: the team name, the <team> in https://<team>.cloudflareaccess.com.
# WARP_CLIENT_ID / WARP_CLIENT_SECRET: a service token from Zero Trust →
# Access controls → Service credentials → Service Tokens (the secret is shown
# once, at creation). The token must be allowed by a device enrollment policy
# whose action is Service Auth, not Allow (Team & Resources → Devices →
# Management → Device enrollment permissions → Manage).
#
# The rig registers a fresh device every run; the org's Settings → WARP
# Client → Device settings decide the tunnel protocol and whether the device
# gets its own local interface IP (100.96/12) or the fixed 172.16.0.2.
WARP_ORG=
WARP_CLIENT_ID=
WARP_CLIENT_SECRET=
